[95.531855, "o", "— 28 tool call(s) so far\r\nAll tasks completed.\r\n\r\n**Files created/updated**\r\n- `/app/active_users_report.json` – 346 active users, sorted by `username`, with `user_id`, `username`, `email`, `last_login` (YYYY-MM-DD), `role_count`, `primary_role` (null when roles empty). Indentation is jq default 2-space.\r\n- `/app/cmd.sh`\r\n```sh\r\njq --arg status active --arg sep T '[ .[] | select(.status==$status) | {user_id: .id, username: .username, email: .email, last_login: (.last_login | split($sep)[0]), role_count: (.roles | length), primary_role: (.roles[0] // null)} ] | sort_by(.username)' /app/users.json > /app/active_users_report.json\r\n```\r\n- `/app/jq_args.yaml`\r\n```yaml\r\nfilter: '[ .[] | select(.status==$status) | {user_id: .id, username: .username, email: .email, last_login: (.last_login | split($sep)[0]), role_count: (.roles | length), primary_role: (.roles[0] // null)} ] | sort_by(.username)'\r\nargs:\r\n  - \"--arg status active\"\r\n  - \"--arg sep T\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nVerification:\r\n```bash\r\nbash /app/cmd.sh\r\njq $(yq -r '.ar"]
[95.531903, "o", "gs[]' /app/jq_args.yaml) \"$(yq -r '.filter' /app/jq_args.yaml)\" /app/users.json > /app/active_users_report.json\r\n```\r\nBoth produce identical output, first user `acosta`, last user `zwelch`, and `role_count`/`primary_role` are correct for empty roles e.g. `alyssasanders` → `role_count:0`, `primary_role:null`.\r\n\r\n\r\n[result] role=implementor model=glimmer-30b tools=28 surface=a148f33da19b\r\n"]
